2026-05-30T17:55Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Source
Path A UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Medium**

## Context
`erg log --help` documents that LINE must follow `actor verb [detail]` format
(e.g. "claude note retried with narrower scope"). The help text says this is
"enforced by erg validate (rule 11)". But when the agent ran:
```
erg log 0001 "decided to use JWT tokens"
```
(no actor, no verb — just a plain sentence), the command succeeded and
`erg validate` passed. Rule 11 is documented but not enforced.

This means users accumulate malformed log entries silently, and audit tools
or future parsing will find inconsistent data.

## Fix
Either:
1. Enforce rule 11 in `erg validate`: fail on log lines that don't match
   `TIMESTAMP ACTOR VERB [DETAIL]` format. (Preferred — keeps the spec honest.)
2. If enforcement is out of scope, remove the "enforced by erg validate" claim
   from the help text and spec, and document the format as convention only.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg validate` fails (or warns) on log lines missing actor+verb, OR
- [ ] Help text and spec updated to say the format is a convention, not enforced
